.TH LIBRDP-WORKSPACE 1 "2026-07-19" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-workspace \- fetch an RDS workspace feed and launch selected resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-workspace
.B --feed
.I url
[
.B --user
.I name
] [
.B --password
.I value
] [
.B --password-env
.I name
] [
.B --domain
.I name
] [
.B --timeout
.I ms
] [
.B --select
.I id|index|title|alias
] [
.B --viewer
.I path
] [
.B --security
.I auto|rdp|tls|nla
] [
.B --launch
] [
.B --no-window
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-workspace
loads a workspace feed through the public librdp workspace API, prints the published desktop and RemoteApp resources, and can start
.BR librdp-viewer (1)
for one selected entry.
.P
When an embedded RDP file contains a gateway host, the launcher passes it to the viewer as Microsoft RD Gateway HTTP transport.
.P
The native window displays the fetched resources and launches the selected
entry. The X11 frontend supports keyboard selection and the Cocoa frontend uses
an AppKit summary window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --feed " url"
Workspace feed URL to fetch. This option is required.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
User name for the feed request and for the viewer launch.
.TP
.BI --password " value"
Password for the feed request and for the viewer launch.
.TP
.BI --password-env " name"
Read the password from an environment variable.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Authentication domain for the feed request and for the viewer launch.
.TP
.BI --timeout " ms"
Feed request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.BI --select " id|index|title|alias"
Select a feed resource by zero-based index, id, title, or alias. Headless launch requires an explicit selection when the feed contains more than one resource.
.TP
.BI --viewer " path"
Viewer executable to launch. The default is
.BR librdp-viewer .
.TP
.BI --security " auto|rdp|tls|nla"
Security mode passed to the viewer. The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.B --launch
Start the selected resource without opening the workspace window.
.TP
.B --no-window
Fetch and print the feed without opening a native window.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Feed processing and optional viewer launch succeeded.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line or workspace configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Feed fetch or resource processing failed.
.TP
.B 4
Viewer launch or native presentation failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
librdp-workspace --feed https://rds.example.com/RDWeb/Feed/webfeed.aspx --user workspace-user --password-env RDS_PASSWORD
librdp-workspace --feed https://rds.example.com/RDWeb/Feed/webfeed.aspx --select 0 --launch --viewer build/librdp-viewer
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Workspace feeds are untrusted launch metadata. The tool only passes the selected target and RemoteApp identifier to the viewer, but deployments should still restrict trusted feed URLs and avoid logging passwords.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp-workspace (7),
.BR librdp-viewer (1),
.BR librdp (7)
